Chapter: TreeViewNav
  cites UI chapter TreeView
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Theme
  cites UI chapter KeyInput

 TrackerApp's project sidebar is a TreeView, and ItemDesignerApp, CallPage
 and diagram's Toolbar each build one. None of them had a test.

 The chapter divides cleanly into what the one live caller reaches and
 what it does not. TrackerApp builds a tree and renders it, so
 construction, depth assignment, the flatten and the widget rows are live.
 Expanding, selecting and navigating are reached by nothing, which is
 exactly why they are asked here: a function nobody calls that is wrong is
 a trap laid for its first caller, and this chapter's whole purpose is
 that a tree can be opened.

 The tree below is three levels deep on one branch and one level on
 another, so a flatten that returned everything and a flatten that
 honoured the expanded flags are visibly different, and so are pre-order
 and any other order.

 We say:

Section: Reading

  at : WidgetNode, Integer -> WidgetNode
  at (w) (i) = list-at (w.wn-children) i

  payload : WidgetNode -> Text
  payload (w) = when w.wn-kind
    is WkLabel (t) -> "[" & t & "]"
    is WkButton (t) -> "<" & t & ">"
    is WkGauge (v) (m) -> "gauge"
    is WkInput (t) (c) -> "input"
    is WkSeparator -> "sep"
    is WkPanel -> "panel"
    is WkCustom (tag) -> tag

  state-name : Integer -> Text
  state-name (s) =
    if s == state-normal then "normal"
    else if s == state-hover then "hover"
    else if s == state-pressed then "pressed"
    else if s == state-focused then "focused"
    else "other"

  ids : List TreeNode -> Text
  ids (ns) = ids-loop ns 0 (list-length ns) ""

  ids-loop : List TreeNode, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  ids-loop (ns) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let node = list-at ns i
    in ids-loop ns (i + 1) n (acc & (if i > 0 then " " else "") & node.tn-id & show (node.tn-depth))

Section: The tree under test

 a has two children; a-1 itself has a child. b is a leaf. c has one child.

  build : Integer -> TreeViewState
  build (x) = tree-view-new "tv" [
    tree-node "a" "Alpha" "A" [
      tree-node "a-1" "Alpha One" "1" [
        tree-node-leaf "a-1-x" "Deep" "x"
      ],
      tree-node-leaf "a-2" "Alpha Two" "2"
    ],
    tree-node-leaf "b" "Bravo" "B",
    tree-node "c" "Charlie" "C" [
      tree-node-leaf "c-1" "Charlie One" "1"
    ]
  ]

Section: Construction and depth

  line-new : Text =
    "new: " & format-tree-view (build 0)

 Depth is assigned at construction and every row's indent is computed from
 it, so it is read at all three levels rather than at the roots only.

  line-depths : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-expand-all (build 0)
    in "depths: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)

Section: What is visible

  line-collapsed : Text =
    "collapsed: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes (build 0))

  line-one-open : Text =
    "a open: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a"))

  line-two-open : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-toggle (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a") "a-1"
    in "a and a-1 open: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)

 Toggling a node whose parent is shut must still flip the node, or opening
 the parent afterwards shows it shut.

  line-nested-first : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-toggle (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a-1") "a"
    in "a-1 opened before a: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)

  line-toggle-twice : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-toggle (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a") "a"
    in "a toggled twice: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)

  line-expand-all : Text =
    "expand-all: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes (tree-view-expand-all (build 0)))

  line-collapse-all : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-collapse-all (tree-view-expand-all (build 0))
    in "collapse-all: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)

Section: Selection

  sel-of : TreeViewState -> Text
  sel-of (tv) =
    let vis = tree-view-visible-nodes (tree-view-expand-all tv)
    in sel-loop vis 0 (list-length vis) ""

  sel-loop : List TreeNode, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  sel-loop (ns) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let node = list-at ns i
    in sel-loop ns (i + 1) n (acc & (if node.tn-selected then node.tn-id & " " else ""))

  line-select : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-select (tree-view-expand-all (build 0)) "a-1-x"
    in "select a-1-x: selected=[" & sel-of tv & "] focused=" & tv.tv-focused-id

 Selecting a second node must leave exactly one selected, or every click
 adds another and nothing ever deselects.

  line-select-twice : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-select (tree-view-select (tree-view-expand-all (build 0)) "a-1-x") "c"
    in "then select c: selected=[" & sel-of tv & "] focused=" & tv.tv-focused-id

Section: What a caller still holding the tree sees

 Both of these hand back a state, so a caller holding the one it passed in
 must find it as it left it.

 The original is read AFTER the call, never before: a snapshot taken first
 records what the tree was and can never disagree with itself.

  line-alias-toggle : Text =
    let tv = build 0
    in let opened = tree-view-toggle tv "a"
    in "alias toggle: returned=" & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes opened)
    & " original-after=" & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)

 And the whole tree is walked, not the roots: the node under test is two
 levels down, so a top-level scan reports nothing selected whatever
 happened.

  line-alias-select : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-expand-all (build 0)
    in let picked = tree-view-select tv "a-1-x"
    in "alias select: returned=[" & sel-of picked & "] original-after=[" & sel-of tv & "]"

Section: The keyboard

 UI chapter KeyInput settles what a key is in this quire: a character is
 its CCE code point and a named key is a constant above key-named-base.
 A handler testing 38 and 40 is reading Windows virtual key codes, and 38
 and 40 are letters in CCE.

  key-walk : Integer, Text -> Text
  key-walk (k) (label) =
    let tv = tree-view-handle-key (tree-view-select (build 0) "a") k
    in label & "=[" & tv.tv-focused-id & "]"

  line-keys : Text =
    "keys: " & key-walk key-down "down" & " " & key-walk key-up "up"
    & " " & key-walk key-right "right"

  line-keys-open : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-handle-key (tree-view-select (build 0) "a") key-right
    in "key-right opens: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)

Section: Navigation

 A fresh tree has no focus. The first Down keypress is therefore the case
 that matters most and the one a test written from the middle of a session
 never reaches.

  line-nav-fresh : Text =
    let one = tree-view-nav-down (build 0)
    in let two = tree-view-nav-down (tree-view-nav-down (build 0))
    in "nav-down from no focus: [" & one.tv-focused-id & "] then again: [" & two.tv-focused-id & "]"

  line-nav-up-fresh : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-nav-up (build 0)
    in "nav-up from no focus: [" & tv.tv-focused-id & "]"

  line-nav-walk : Text =
    let one = tree-view-nav-down (tree-view-select (build 0) "a")
    in let two = tree-view-nav-down (tree-view-select (build 0) "b")
    in "walk: from a -> [" & one.tv-focused-id & "] from b -> [" & two.tv-focused-id & "]"

  line-nav-ends : Text =
    let last = tree-view-nav-down (tree-view-select (build 0) "c")
    in let first = tree-view-nav-up (tree-view-select (build 0) "a")
    in "ends: down at last -> [" & last.tv-focused-id & "] up at first -> [" & first.tv-focused-id & "]"

  line-nav-into : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-nav-down (tree-view-select (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a") "a")
    in "down into an open branch: [" & tv.tv-focused-id & "]"

Section: Left, which does two jobs

  line-left-open : Text =
    let tv = tv-collapse-or-parent (tree-view-select (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a") "a")
    in "left on an open node: " & ids (tree-view-visible-nodes tv) & " focus=" & tv.tv-focused-id

  line-left-child : Text =
    let tv = tv-collapse-or-parent (tree-view-select (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a") "a-2")
    in "left on a child: focus=" & tv.tv-focused-id

  line-left-root : Text =
    let tv = tv-collapse-or-parent (tree-view-select (build 0) "b")
    in "left on a shut root: focus=" & tv.tv-focused-id

 The parent walk is reached from `tv-collapse-or-parent` only for a node
 that was found, so a missing focus cannot arrive through that door. It is
 a published name and a citing chapter can call it, so it is called here
 with a tree that has no focus at all.

 This line pins the ANSWER and not the guard, and the difference is worth
 being plain about: deleting the bounds check in `tv-go-parent` does not
 move this line, because the parent search refuses a start of -1 by
 itself. The guard exists to stop the read that happens first, which would
 take `list-at` one below element zero and land on the list's capacity
 cell. Nothing this harness can print distinguishes the two, and saying so
 here is better than leaving a guard that looks tested.

  line-parent-unfocused : Text =
    let tv = build 0
    in let moved = tv-go-parent tv (tree-view-visible-nodes tv)
    in "parent with no focus: focus=[" & moved.tv-focused-id & "]"

Section: The rows TrackerApp actually draws

 A fresh tree renders its roots and nothing else, which is what the one
 live caller shows. Each row is an indent, an expander, an icon and a
 label, so the expander glyph is what says whether a branch can be opened.

  row-of : WidgetNode, Integer -> WidgetNode
  row-of (t) (i) = at t i

  row-text : WidgetNode, Integer -> Text
  row-text (t) (i) =
    let r = row-of t i
    in r.wn-id & " " & payload (at r 0) & payload (at r 1) & payload (at r 2) & payload (at r 3)

  line-rows : Text =
    let t = tree-view-widget (build 0)
    in "rows=" & show (t.wn-child-count) & " " & row-text t 0 & " " & row-text t 1

  line-rows-open : Text =
    let t = tree-view-widget (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a")
    in "open rows=" & show (t.wn-child-count) & " " & row-text t 0 & " " & row-text t 1

  line-row-states : Text =
    let tv = tree-view-select (build 0) "b"
    in let t = tree-view-widget tv
    in "states: a=" & state-name ((row-of t 0).wn-state)
    & " b=" & state-name ((row-of t 1).wn-state)
    & " c=" & state-name ((row-of t 2).wn-state)

  line-format-node : Text =
    let vis = tree-view-visible-nodes (tree-view-select (tree-view-toggle (build 0) "a") "a")
    in "format: [" & format-tree-node (list-at vis 0) & "] [" & format-tree-node (list-at vis 1) & "]"

Section: Body

  report-a : Text =
    line-new & "\n" & line-depths & "\n" & line-collapsed & "\n" & line-one-open
    & "\n" & line-two-open & "\n" & line-nested-first & "\n" & line-toggle-twice

  report-b : Text =
    line-expand-all & "\n" & line-collapse-all & "\n" & line-select & "\n" & line-select-twice
    & "\n" & line-alias-toggle & "\n" & line-alias-select
    & "\n" & line-keys & "\n" & line-keys-open

  report-c : Text =
    line-nav-fresh & "\n" & line-nav-up-fresh & "\n" & line-nav-walk
    & "\n" & line-nav-ends & "\n" & line-nav-into

  report-d : Text =
    line-left-open & "\n" & line-left-child & "\n" & line-left-root
    & "\n" & line-parent-unfocused

  report-e : Text =
    line-rows & "\n" & line-rows-open & "\n" & line-row-states & "\n" & line-format-node

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni report-a
    print-line-uni report-b
    print-line-uni report-c
    print-line-uni report-d
    print-line-uni report-e
  end
